Selection + ordering reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform parity, NOT a "corrected"
version):
  recent = data.achievements
             .filter(a => a.unlocked && a.unlocked_at)        // unlocked + has unlock time only
             .sort((a,b) => Date.parse(b.unlocked_at) - Date.parse(a.unlocked_at))   // desc, STABLE
             .slice(0, limit)                                  // limit = (cols>=3) ? 5 : 3
  Stability: web Array.prototype.sort is stable (ES2019+); reproduced with an `offset` tiebreaker so
             equal unlock instants keep original payload order (not Swift's unspecified sort stability).
  Opt-out : !useAchievementCelebrationPrefs().showOnDashboard → "disabled" empty state (widget slot
            stays in the grid). Coalesced into the P1/S8 snapshot (showOnDashboard), not read in the view.
  Deep link: each badge tap → onOpen(id) → web navigate('/lifetime?achievement={id}').
  i18n keys (parity): widget.recentlyUnlocked.title/disabled · achievements.viewNamed ({{name}}→%@) ·
            achievements.noneYet · lifetime.unlocked · widget.recentlyUnlocked(.description) [registry].

